IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- PART 12, REGISTERS, RETURNS AND OTHER
-- DOCUMENTARY REQUIREMENTS, ss 95 to 96A.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- Part 12 is where the Act becomes checkable in practice: employee records, a
-- written record of key employment terms, and a pay slip. Without these the
-- rest of the Act is hard to enforce, because the employee has no evidence of
-- what was agreed or paid.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 97 to 101 (returns, the Commissioner's powers to call for
-- further returns and for books, and the offence provision). Almost every
-- period in this Part is "the period prescribed", so the regulations carry the
-- numbers and were not retrieved; the one number stated in the Act itself is
-- the 14 days in s 95A(2).

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 12`

§§ `95 -- Employee records`

-- s 95(1): "An employer MUST make, and keep for THE PERIOD PRESCRIBED ...,
-- employee records containing the prescribed particulars for -- (a) every
-- employee the employer employs; and (b) EVERY FORMER EMPLOYEE of the
-- employer."
--
-- The duty reaches former employees, which is what makes the retention period
-- matter. The period itself is prescribed and is not in the Act.
--
-- s 95(2): the record must be "READILY ACCESSIBLE to the employee or former
-- employee to which the employee record relates" throughout that period.
--
-- s 95(3): "An employer is TAKEN TO HAVE FAILED to comply with subsection (1)
-- if the employer makes or keeps an employee record that is INCOMPLETE OR
-- INACCURATE, WHETHER OR NOT THE EMPLOYER KNEW". A deeming provision with no
-- mental element: the state of the record is the breach.
DECLARE EmployeeRecord HAS
    `the person is an employee or a former employee of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a record was made`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record contains the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record has been kept throughout the prescribed record retention period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record is readily accessible to the employee or former employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record is incomplete or inaccurate`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer knew it was incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the record` IS AN EmployeeRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has complied with section 95(1)` IF
        `the record`'s `a record was made`
    AND `the record`'s `the record contains the prescribed particulars`
    AND `the record`'s `the record has been kept throughout the prescribed record retention period`
    AND NOT `section 95(3) deems a failure` `the record`

-- s 95(3), stated on its own because the absence of a mental element is the
-- point: knowledge is irrelevant.
GIVEN `the record` IS AN EmployeeRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 95(3) deems a failure` IF
    `the record`'s `the record is incomplete or inaccurate`

GIVEN `the record` IS AN EmployeeRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has complied with section 95(2)` IF
    `the record`'s `the record is readily accessible to the employee or former employee`

§§ `95A -- The written record of key employment terms`

-- s 95A(1): the section applies only to an employee who (a) entered into the
-- contract of service ON OR AFTER 1 APRIL 2016, and (b) is employed under it
-- "for a period NOT SHORTER THAN the prescribed minimum period of service."
--
-- s 95A(2): the employer "must give each employee ... a WRITTEN RECORD of the
-- key employment terms NOT LATER THAN 14 DAYS after the day that the employee
-- starts employment ..., or within such other period as may be prescribed in
-- substitution."
`the key employment terms deadline in days` MEANS 14

DECLARE KeyTermsFacts HAS
    `the contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a written record of the key employment terms was given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the start of employment when it was given` IS A NUMBER
    `another period has been prescribed in substitution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the substituted period in days`            IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the facts` IS A KeyTermsFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 95A applies to the employee` IF
        `the facts`'s `the contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016`
    AND `the facts`'s `employed for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A KeyTermsFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the period allowed for the key employment terms` IS
    IF   `the facts`'s `another period has been prescribed in substitution`
    THEN `the facts`'s `the substituted period in days`
    ELSE `the key employment terms deadline in days`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A KeyTermsFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has contravened section 95A` IF
        `section 95A applies to the employee` `the facts`
    AND `the record was not given in time` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A KeyTermsFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record was not given in time` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `a written record of the key employment terms was given`
    OR  `the facts`'s `days after the start of employment when it was given`
            GREATER THAN `the period allowed for the key employment terms` `the facts`

§§ `96 -- Pay slips`

-- s 96(1): the employer must give (a) every employee a pay slip, "within the
-- time prescribed", for all salary paid for the salary period; and (b) a pay
-- slip for every sum paid under s 22 (payment on dismissal) or s 23 (payment on
-- termination by the employee).
--
-- s 96(3): the duty is satisfied by an ELECTRONIC RECORD provided in a manner
-- that lets the employee access and use it "for subsequent reference".
--
-- s 96(4): the same deeming as s 95(3) -- an incomplete or inaccurate pay slip
-- is a failure to comply, knowledge irrelevant.
DECLARE PaySlipFacts HAS
    `a pay slip was given for the salary period`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pay slip was given for a sum paid under section 22 or 23` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a sum was paid under section 22 or 23`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `given within the time prescribed`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the prescribed form and containing the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given as an electronic record accessible and useable for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer is exempted by an order under section 96(5)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 96(3) means a paper slip is not required: either route satisfies (1).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A PaySlipFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a pay slip was given in an acceptable form` IF
        `the facts`'s `a pay slip was given for the salary period`
    OR  `the facts`'s `given as an electronic record accessible and useable for subsequent reference`

-- s 96(1)(b): the second pay slip is owed only where a s 22 or s 23 sum was in
-- fact paid.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A PaySlipFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 96(1)(b) pay slip is owed` IF
    `the facts`'s `a sum was paid under section 22 or 23`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PaySlipFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has complied with section 96` IF
        `the facts`'s `the employer is exempted by an order under section 96(5)`
    OR  `every pay slip requirement is met` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PaySlipFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every pay slip requirement is met` IF
        `a pay slip was given in an acceptable form` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `given within the time prescribed`
    AND `the facts`'s `in the prescribed form and containing the prescribed information`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate`
    AND `the termination pay slip, where owed, was given` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PaySlipFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the termination pay slip, where owed, was given` IF
        NOT `the section 96(1)(b) pay slip is owed` `the facts`
    OR  `the facts`'s `a pay slip was given for a sum paid under section 22 or 23`
